          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p><fr:link href="/OGCRN/" title="Vector Processing Unit" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/OGCRN/" display-uri="OGCRN" type="local">Vector Processing Unit</fr:link>: what is its shape and throughput relative to the <fr:link href="/OGCRP/" title="Matrix Multiply Unit (MXU)" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/OGCRP/" display-uri="OGCRP" type="local">Matrix Multiply Unit (MXU)</fr:link>, and which reductions are cheap?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  Shape <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(8\ \text {sublanes}, 128\ \text {lanes})]]></fr:tex>, with 4 independent ALUs per position and most ops at 1/cycle:

  <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[8 \times  128 \times  4 \times  1.75\mathrm {e}9 \approx  7\mathrm {e}12 \text { FLOPs/s}]]></fr:tex>

  on v5p — about <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[30\times ]]></fr:tex> less than the ~<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[2e14]]></fr:tex> MXU FLOPs/s per core. VPU work is fp32.

  <html:strong>Reductions</html:strong> along the <html:strong>sublane</html:strong> axis (the 8) are cheap: an intra-lane shuffle by 4/2/1 plus three pairwise adds. <html:strong>Cross-lane</html:strong> reductions need the separate XLU, which is slow and expensive.

  Control is skewed the other way: a single <fr:link href="/WY6L/" title="Scalar core (TPU)" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/WY6L/" display-uri="WY6L" type="local">scalar core</fr:link> fetches and dispatches everything and can issue only <html:strong>one DMA request per cycle</html:strong>. Efficient, but it blocks data-dependent vectorization.
</html:details>
</html:div>



